{"_id":"72e4e2c4-017f-4e12-a397-534c1aee2614","author":null,"body":[{"_key":"8a548e17accf","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"fffd93ff6f49","_type":"span","marks":["em"],"text":"Your developer isn't trying to confuse you. But, more often than not, there's a gap between what they assume you know and what you actually know about building an efficient, value-added, and scalable digital product, especially for your specific project."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"cde26751d7cb","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"44f06dc8d117","_type":"span","marks":["em"],"text":"Don’t worry, you don't need to learn coding or sweat the technical details. You already have enough on your plate, juggling your core professional roles and running a business (after all, that’s why you hired them in the first place)."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"02e3dab3714d","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"6036bdbba773","_type":"span","marks":["em"],"text":"But here’s the part that matters: having a basic understanding of these seven truths will help you ask better questions, spot red flags early, and make smarter decisions that protect your investment. So let’s cut through the jargon."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"eede473ab458","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"48140fe8b6d1","_type":"span","marks":["em"],"text":"These are the things that often go unsaid."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"e80950afc4f4","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"ce8bd9c8efba","_type":"span","marks":["strong"],"text":"Your product will need updates and fixes after launch"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"065a49471baa","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"60661b5c7f18","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Launching your product is just the starting point. To stay competitive and profitable, it needs ongoing improvement—whether that’s refining user experience, adding new features, or incorporating customer feedback. Regular updates also build trust signals: publishing fresh blog posts, refreshing content across key pages, and aligning with Google’s preference for dynamic sites."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"5fa5df75da93","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"339aa09c46ed","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"However, these improvements need not happen overnight. Think of them as part of a planned cycle. Imagine your digital product as a living system—one that grows these pipelines."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"826069b39585","_type":"image","asset":{"_ref":"image-38f187f1758218f8338b22eb5651e85e006ddbdc-626x417-png","_type":"reference"}},{"_key":"716317a910d3","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"37f327f56cf3","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"The key is to avoid constant “quick changes” mid-project. Stick to the approved prototypes, launch smoothly, then plan structured updates that keep your product agile without disrupting timelines or budgets. This also means thinking of your developer as a long-term partner, not a one-off vendor. That partnership ensures your product evolves, scales, and keeps delivering value well beyond its first release."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"d5e276e93e55","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"3b65cf2a32f0","_type":"span","marks":["strong"],"text":"A website isn’t the same as a web app"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"3c482e5fb95a","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"7c2b5734a18f","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"It’s easy to assume that “website” and “web app” mean the same thing, but they serve very different purposes. A website is primarily informational—it’s designed to present content, showcase your brand, and provide static resources like articles, service pages, or contact details. A web app, on the other hand, is interactive. It’s built to perform tasks, process data, and enable users to take action, whether that’s booking a service, managing accounts, or collaborating in real time."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"4e764bfcc057","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"c7b873766ff0","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"For decision makers, the distinction matters because it directly impacts cost, complexity, and scalability. A web app requires deeper engineering, ongoing maintenance, and often integration with other systems. Treating it like a simple website can lead to underestimating timelines, budgets, and the level of support needed."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"b412b9a25ead","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"c971ece2b965","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"The takeaway: be clear on what you’re building. If your product needs functionality beyond static content, you’re not just commissioning a website—you’re investing in a digital platform that demands a more strategic, long-term approach."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"a01c454e7329","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"044a6f8f04e7","_type":"span","marks":["strong"],"text":"Security doesn’t happen by default"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"613b09ce06fb","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"d52c3dab0b8a","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"It’s tempting to assume that once your product is built, it’s automatically secure. The truth is, security has to be engineered deliberately—it doesn’t come “out of the box.” Every digital product, whether a website, mobile app, or enterprise platform, is exposed to risks ranging from data breaches to unauthorized access. Without a clear security strategy, you’re leaving doors open."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"c59dc60774b5","_type":"image","asset":{"_ref":"image-1b3e1012ca5ec5f99e230fb50cb7f16a152d1061-626x417-png","_type":"reference"}},{"_key":"ed23e5cea96e","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"994000be7513","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Strong security means more than installing firewalls or SSL certificates. It involves practices like encrypting sensitive data, managing user permissions, monitoring for suspicious activity, and keeping software dependencies up to date. It also means planning for compliance if you operate in regulated industries. According to IBM’s "},{"_key":"31fc3037018f","_type":"span","marks":["bbfaacb59d39"],"text":"Cost of a Data Breach Report 2025"},{"_key":"6dab78267663","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":", the average breach costs organizations millions—proof that prevention is far cheaper than recovery."}],"markDefs":[{"_key":"bbfaacb59d39","_type":"link","href":"https://www.ibm.com/reports/data-breach"}],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"810eb946e2d5","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"66eb50039c70","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"In essence, as a product owner, security should be part of your product roadmap from day one. Partner with developers who treat it as a continuous process, not a checkbox, so your product can grow confidently without exposing your business to unnecessary risk."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"889d144182a3","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"702ba76de33d","_type":"span","marks":["strong"],"text":"Good testing takes time and prevents costly disasters"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"081763d7b115","_type":"image","asset":{"_ref":"image-b52b1ad2bf15926d4ca5a0bdeeb538f89da008c4-5472x3648-jpg","_type":"reference"}},{"_key":"5ec78bea768b","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"72322b68042c","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"One of the easiest traps to fall into is rushing a product to launch without giving testing the attention it deserves. Proper testing isn’t just about catching bugs—it’s about protecting your investment. It ensures your product works as intended across devices, browsers, and user scenarios, and that it can handle real-world stress without breaking."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"19b5937a3aa2","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"196f0907da10","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Skipping or rushing this stage often leads to expensive fixes later: downtime, broken features, frustrated customers, or even reputational damage. In fact, studies show that the cost of fixing a defect after release can be several times higher than catching it during development. "},{"_key":"96867bb76222","_type":"span","marks":["da412139b2ad"],"text":"Through testing"},{"_key":"744ca9aa40d8","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":" (functional, performance, security, and usability) takes time, but it saves money and headaches in the long run."}],"markDefs":[{"_key":"da412139b2ad","_type":"link","href":"https://www.browserstack.com/guide/types-of-testing"}],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"9471f9fe7d52","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"eeb844f3ad4f","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Testing is not a “nice-to-have.” It’s a critical safeguard. Build it into your timeline, respect the process, and trust your developer when they say it’s worth the wait."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"f001ce3c7abb","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"0cbe8e7c1470","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":""}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"18029dc0492e","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"68930d8b8440","_type":"span","marks":["strong"],"text":"Every “quick change” mid-project increases cost and time"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"6b24e86e3043","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"d85f987b80dc","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"It’s natural to spot new ideas or tweaks while a project is underway, but every mid‑stream change has a ripple effect. Development teams work from approved prototypes and roadmaps; altering them mid-project often means re‑engineering code, re‑testing features, and re‑aligning timelines. What feels like a “small adjustment” can quickly add unexpected costs and delays."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"01a306572d71","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"d3ee2ffc6415","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"The smarter approach is to let the build follow the agreed plan, launch smoothly, and then schedule improvements in structured update cycles. This way, feedback and new ideas are incorporated without derailing progress."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"04b55ef7b4f7","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"4cf67d1c0bf4","_type":"span","marks":["strong"],"text":"If it doesn't work on mobile, you're invisible to most customers"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"963709fa123c","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"e4fd2d120056","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Today, mobile is the default. As of 2025, over "},{"_key":"2ad741d68b1a","_type":"span","marks":["6659cce9b48b"],"text":"64% of global web traffi"},{"_key":"c5543f81ac35","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"c comes from mobile devices, and for many users, it’s their only way to access the internet. If your product isn’t optimized for mobile—fast loading, responsive layouts, intuitive navigation—you risk losing the majority of your audience before they even engage. Worse still, research shows that 40% of users will switch to a competitor after a poor mobile experience, underscoring its direct impact on "},{"_key":"065e890a8bf4","_type":"span","marks":["fd09ab27ba06"],"text":"retention and conversions"},{"_key":"271011a57356","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"."}],"markDefs":[{"_key":"6659cce9b48b","_type":"link","href":"https://www.statista.com/statistics/277125/share-of-website-traffic-coming-from-mobile-devices/"},{"_key":"fd09ab27ba06","_type":"link","href":"https://uxcam.com/blog/ux-statistics/"}],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"7a5dee480b1f","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"8f9ddf5cc11a","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Mobile readiness goes beyond shrinking a desktop site to fit a smaller screen. It’s about designing experiences that feel natural in the palm of a hand: touch‑friendly buttons, streamlined forms, and content that’s easy to read on the go. Google also uses "},{"_key":"4321cc46abcc","_type":"span","marks":["78d2ecd6db6f"],"text":"mobile‑first indexing"},{"_key":"8b8583778eb0","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":" for search rankings, meaning sites that aren’t mobile‑friendly lose visibility and credibility.The takeaway: mobile optimization is the foundation of customer trust, SEO success, and long‑term growth in a market where mobile is the primary access point for browsing, researching, and buying."}],"markDefs":[{"_key":"78d2ecd6db6f","_type":"link","href":"https://developers.google.com/search/docs/crawling-indexing/mobile/mobile-sites-mobile-first-indexing"}],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"7f06b4ca5608","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"62fc696d713b","_type":"span","marks":["strong"],"text":"Knowing the basics of UX, UI, and SEO helps you make better decisions"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"eb1545e22674","_type":"image","asset":{"_ref":"image-4e450cad6fa78c10022bb6d00c311cfa592d6251-3000x2000-jpg","_type":"reference"}},{"_key":"77363c993302","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"2bab262ec0cf","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"You don’t need to be a designer or marketer to appreciate how user experience (UX), user interface (UI), and search engine optimization (SEO) shape the success of your digital product. A basic understanding of these three areas helps you ask sharper questions, evaluate trade‑offs, and avoid decisions that look good on paper but fail in practice."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"cf17a9bf96aa","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"0ca05d65a874","_type":"span","marks":["strong"],"text":"UX"},{"_key":"3e09cb3b7151","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":" is about how people feel when using your product. Poor UX frustrates users and drives them away, while thoughtful UX builds loyalty."}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"998722f53dc3","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"5d527a3c04da","_type":"span","marks":["strong"],"text":"UI"},{"_key":"b9e734d660b9","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":" is the visual layer, such as colors, typography, layouts, and interactions. Clean, consistent UI makes your product intuitive and trustworthy."}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"1fdcb76558a2","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"55b9926ed1b0","_type":"span","marks":["strong"],"text":"SEO"},{"_key":"596288159a6c","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":" ensures your product can be found. Google’s algorithms reward sites with relevant content, fast performance, and mobile‑friendly design. Without SEO, even the best product risks invisibility."}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"a0200c49f637","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"a3f3f63f6cab","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Knowing these basics means you can balance aesthetics with usability, and visibility with performance. It’s about making informed choices that keep your product competitive, discoverable, and user‑friendly."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"b8af4d0b52c1","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"f4cb6a63dfd8","_type":"span","marks":["strong"],"text":"So, what next?"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h2"},{"_key":"aaa54c1d0165","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"5d56a30147d6","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"If you’ve grasped even half of these truths, you’re already ahead of many digital product owners. Not because you’re suddenly technical, but because you’re informed; and informed leaders make smarter, more confident choices."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"eaa92ad75b10","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"8aa76d56423c","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"At "},{"_key":"bd2c287bbd3b","_type":"span","marks":["92580a36de7e"],"text":"Tekfolio"},{"_key":"962cfacc0c8e","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":", we believe the best e-products are born where business clarity meets solid engineering. Our role isn’t just to write code; it’s to guide you through why certain decisions matter, so nothing feels confusing, rushed, or out of control."}],"markDefs":[{"_key":"92580a36de7e","_type":"link","href":"https://tekfolio.ng/contact"}],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"e0b5963bb131","_type":"image","asset":{"_ref":"image-5a62dc933b3e1e1031b844832a4aff8b080ed331-626x417-png","_type":"reference"}},{"_key":"5e80c56b6d78","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"74edd272d126","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"That’s the difference between a one‑off launch and a long‑term asset. With the right perspective and the right partner, your product does more than just go live. It grows, adapts, and keeps delivering value long after day one."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"5683f075e29f","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"65fe6f53f288","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"\n"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"}],"categories":[{"_id":"a23e556d-33da-4aef-a6cc-1b6b0cbf7c7b","slug":null,"title":"web development"},{"_id":"a9506ad7-45c4-4038-8afc-aaf3808df0ea","slug":null,"title":"client relationship"},{"_id":"44f77539-6466-4a11-b018-0bb514fa6ec3","slug":null,"title":"UI UX Design"}],"excerpt":" With the right perspective and the right partner, your product grows, adapts, and continues to deliver value long after day one.\n","mainImage":{"alt":"Having a basic understanding of a few facts will help you make smarter decisions ","asset":{"_ref":"image-e5a17193b00602962a90dd728fd761891a6f6492-2000x1791-jpg","_type":"reference"}},"publishedAt":"2025-12-22T08:56:54.969Z","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"7-things-your-developer-might-not-tell-you-but-you-should-know"},"title":"7 Things Your Developer Might Not Tell You (But You Should Know)"}